          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observed in the sky on September 17, 2014, around 5 PM, a round, red object that seemed to rotate on itself, resembling a saucer. Observing a flying object in a straight line with the wind suggests a balloon carried by the wind, likely a latex or mylar balloon. The local wind in Nice is from the east, consistent with the object's movement towards the west (see: weather). The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a child's balloon.",
